WEBVTT

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:24.270
Ooh!

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.340
You can see it now, Regina.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:29.680
That place with all the lights
is Kuchiba City.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.230
I bet you’ll make
lots of friends there.

00:00:33.770 --> 00:00:35.220
I already...

00:00:35.810 --> 00:00:36.520
Hmm?

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:38.810
Nothing.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:47.690
Take care out there!

00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.700
See you later.

00:00:49.700 --> 00:00:51.700
Come on, Satoshi,
just enjoy yourself!

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.400
I don’t see this going well...

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.650
It’ll be fine!

00:00:54.650 --> 00:00:58.020
I’ll tell them all about
what makes you so awesome!

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:00.320
That’s what
I’m worried about...

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.710
Relax, relax!
Trust me on this one!

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.830
When I heard the topic was people you’re friends with,
your face immediately sprung to mind.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:12.090
Guess that makes sense.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:15.780
Still, going to school with you
feels a little weird...

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:19.640
Come on, seeing you in person
is the best way for them to see how funny you are.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:21.170
“Funny...”?

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:23.390
You’re hilarious, Satoshi!

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:25.060
“Hilarious,” huh?

00:01:27.410 --> 00:01:29.100
Friends...

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:30.830
I’m happy for you, Go.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:40.960
A Glacia?

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:46.250
How lovely!

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.720
Glacia. Fresh Snow Pokémon.
Ice type.

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:54.410
One of Eevee’s
possible evolutions.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:02:00.850
By controlling its body heat, it can freeze
the atmosphere around it to make a diamond-dust flurry.

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:03.400
What is it, Mieze?

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.100
Let go.

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.610
Mieze?

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.360
Hey, Koharu!

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:09.610
We’re gonna leave you behind!

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:11.130
I’m coming!

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:05.140
...and does the inside
of Satoshi’s head look like?

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:10.100
It’s pretty much just stuffed
with Pokémon and Pokémon battles!

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.730
That’s not true!

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:14.210
It is, though.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.580
I think about other stuff, too!

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.630
Like what?

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.770
Like, uh...

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.870
What we’re having
for dinner tonight.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.520
This is more like a comedy act
than a presentation...

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.870
Oh, and this is
the most important point.

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.000
Satoshi can understand
how Pokémon feel!

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:34.650
You can too, though.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.930
Like with Aceburn or Sarunori.

00:04:36.930 --> 00:04:41.490
I think our ways of understanding them
are a bit different.

00:04:41.490 --> 00:04:44.970
You have this sort of...
animal instinct?

00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.350
Animal? Hmm...

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.840
Yeah, I know just what
he means!

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:53.980
And that is all for my presentation
on my friend, Satoshi.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.940
That was a great presentation!

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:06.850
Satoshi, since you’ve come all this way,
you should spend the day here and enjoy yourself.

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:07.750
Sounds good!

00:05:10.180 --> 00:05:11.250
Who’s that?

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:18.060
Good to see you!

00:05:18.060 --> 00:05:19.630
I was getting worried.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:21.320
I’m sorry.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.640
Everyone, this is Regina,
a transfer student!

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.020
She’ll only be here for a short time
while her parents are working here,

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:33.130
but I hope you’ll all
be kind to her.

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:35.020
Yeah!

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:40.200
Regina, here we leave our Pokémon
in the Pokémon Garden.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.030
Can someone show her?

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:43.780
I can find it by myself.

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.950
But we can’t have you
getting lost...

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.030
Miss!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:50.040
I’ll show her!

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:52.550
Thank you.
If you would, then.

00:05:55.280 --> 00:05:56.670
My name’s Koharu.

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.420
Shall we go?

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:05.380
Your Glacia is really pretty.

00:06:07.610 --> 00:06:09.380
What was it, “Mieze”?

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:11.930
How do you know that?

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:14.170
Oh, sorry...

00:06:14.170 --> 00:06:15.810
I happened to see you
this morning.

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.820
I wanted to say hello,
but I lost sight of you.

00:06:19.820 --> 00:06:23.400
So I’m glad to have the chance
to meet you!

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.420
Look, over there
is the Pokémon Garden.

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:36.370
Everyone!

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:41.300
This is my friend Regina,
and her Glacia, Mieze.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.340
Be nice to them.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:48.350
Eevee is my partner, Pikachu is Satoshi’s,
and Sarunori is Go’s.

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.850
Oh, I’ll introduce you
to Satoshi and Go later.

00:07:06.010 --> 00:07:08.370
Hey, let me join in!

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.900
Nice to meet you, Mieze.

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.600
Mieze...

00:07:14.540 --> 00:07:16.100
Wait for me here.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.530
When it’s time to go home...

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:19.330
You can come here
during lunch break!

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.460
When it’s lunch time,
I’ll be back to check on you.

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.640
See you, then!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:41.780
Satoshi and Go live
at my father’s research lab.

00:07:41.780 --> 00:07:43.020
Research lab?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.890
A Pokémon research lab.

00:07:44.890 --> 00:07:47.740
It’s called
the Sakuragi Institute.

00:07:48.340 --> 00:07:49.750
Sakuragi...

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.330
Sakuragi Institute?

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.890
Yes, an institute in Kuchiba City
with a good reputation.

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:01.090
Oh, then that’ll be perfect.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:03.130
We can have them
examine Glacia.

00:08:05.630 --> 00:08:07.620
Oh, welcome back.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:09.750
<i>Regina!</i>

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.930
Where are you from?

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:12.680
How long
are you gonna be here?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.270
I want to know
all about your Glacia!

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.940
C’mon, you guys.
Settle down.

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:49.490
I can’t move!

00:08:49.490 --> 00:08:53.680
Nyah-nyah! Ice Queen!

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:59.270
<i>Ice Queen! Ice Queen! Ice Queen!</i>

00:08:59.270 --> 00:09:04.400
Better watch out!
The Ice Queen can freeze anything!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:08.850
No, I’m not an Ice Queen!

00:09:08.850 --> 00:09:10.150
But you look exactly like her!

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:15.920
<i>Ice Queen! Ice Queen! Ice Queen!</i>

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:21.420
Mieze?

00:09:42.920 --> 00:09:45.310
I’m sorry for freezing you.

00:09:50.140 --> 00:09:51.530
Don’t worry about it!

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:52.590
Right!

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.160
No harm, no foul!

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:00.660
A Glacia?

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:03.670
It has an enormous amount of power
it uses to freeze things.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:05.630
Anything it dislikes,
it freezes.

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:11.910
Which is why she hasn’t been able to make friends,
and has had to transfer schools again and again.

00:10:11.910 --> 00:10:13.680
That must weigh on your mind.

00:10:14.360 --> 00:10:18.890
Professor Sakuragi,
would you consider examining our Glacia?

00:10:18.890 --> 00:10:20.620
We’re worried...

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.940
We don’t know
if we can let them stay together.

00:10:22.940 --> 00:10:26.190
You suspect
there’s something wrong with Glacia?

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:30.050
That’s not something
we can say.

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:30.980
But...

00:10:33.060 --> 00:10:36.200
We want her to have friends!

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.950
As long as Glacia is with her,
she’ll always be alone.

00:10:41.380 --> 00:10:42.810
Please, can you help us?

00:10:47.340 --> 00:10:48.530
Right?

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:01.590
She’s gone...

00:11:01.590 --> 00:11:03.020
That was such a shock...

00:11:07.630 --> 00:11:08.930
Ta-daah!

00:11:09.540 --> 00:11:11.040
Let’s eat lunch together!

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:13.400
With Eevee and Mieze, too!

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.430
Fair enough...
Then how about tomorrow?

00:11:19.430 --> 00:11:21.200
I’ll be gone tomorrow.

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.200
Huh? What do you mean?

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:24.290
Exactly what I said.

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.250
Oh, no...

00:11:26.250 --> 00:11:28.130
But we’ve only just
become friends!

00:11:31.060 --> 00:11:33.270
Mieze is my only friend.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.790
Bye. The teacher wants to see me.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.110
Regina.

00:11:51.110 --> 00:11:52.360
Regina?

00:11:53.170 --> 00:11:54.430
Regina?

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:56.560
Yes?

00:11:56.560 --> 00:11:57.860
Miss!

00:11:58.760 --> 00:11:59.990
Koharu?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.230
And Go, and Satoshi...

00:12:02.230 --> 00:12:02.720
What’s going on—?

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:03.030
We have a request.
What’s going on—?

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:04.120
We have a request.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:07.120
Please don’t kick Regina out!

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:11.510
That Blizzard earlier
was an accident!

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:13.210
I saw it,
so I know what happened!

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:16.220
Glacia was just
trying to protect Regina!

00:12:16.630 --> 00:12:18.000
So please!

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:22.100
Now why would I do that?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:27.210
She just transferred here today,
so there’s a lot she won’t be used to.

00:12:27.210 --> 00:12:30.250
I was just telling her
all about the school.

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:31.340
You were?

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:32.210
Oh, dear.

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:35.230
Weren’t you listening, Regina?

00:12:35.950 --> 00:12:38.950
I thought...
It would be like always...

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.640
Oh, is that all?

00:12:40.640 --> 00:12:43.050
You were fretting
over nothing, Koharu.

00:12:43.050 --> 00:12:43.990
Sorry.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.540
I guess I jumped to conclusions.

00:12:45.910 --> 00:12:47.500
Still, I’m glad she’s okay.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.320
Yeah!

00:12:50.340 --> 00:12:53.040
Let’s eat lunch together!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.170
Come on out, Mieze.

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.100
Mieze, stop!

00:13:14.720 --> 00:13:15.710
Mieze?

00:13:17.600 --> 00:13:19.300
Pocket Monsters.

00:13:34.590 --> 00:13:36.930
Is Mieze going to be okay?

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.910
Don’t worry, don’t worry!

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.440
Koharu’s right!

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:47.940
Leave it to the Director!
It’s gonna be okay!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:51.670
Everyone...

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:54.870
Its condition is stable.

00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:57.230
It should stay here
and rest for today.

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.900
Is Mieze sick?

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:05.290
You’re taking
very good care of Mieze.

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.040
I could tell by seeing
the test results.

00:14:08.490 --> 00:14:09.380
But...

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.360
But?

00:14:10.360 --> 00:14:14.640
This here is its temperature data,
which is alarmingly low.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:20.380
Glacia are known to have low body temperatures,
but this is still far too low.

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:27.180
I hear Mieze has frequently
been making powerful Blizzards.

00:14:27.680 --> 00:14:34.190
It’s likely over-exerting itself and ending up
unable to properly control its body heat.

00:14:34.190 --> 00:14:38.440
If it keeps pushing itself too far,
then Mieze will...

00:14:40.640 --> 00:14:44.070
It’s my fault... It’s...

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.660
Regina...

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.390
The first time Mieze
created a Blizzard like that...

00:14:56.930 --> 00:15:02.980
...was when I was being bullied
for looking like the Ice Queen in a picture book.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:08.090
Then, when similar incidents
happened again and again,

00:15:08.090 --> 00:15:11.620
Mieze would always
come and save me.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:18.440
Not long after, Mieze was always on edge,
making sure nobody tried to hurt me.

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:20.370
Always, constantly.

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:24.170
I knew...

00:15:24.170 --> 00:15:25.780
I knew I shouldn’t...

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:27.530
But I just hid behind it.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:31.650
I’m sorry...
I’m sorry, Mieze!

00:15:31.650 --> 00:15:36.400
You’ve always protected me,
but I never did the same for you...

00:15:36.400 --> 00:15:39.000
That’s not
what a friend would do...

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.800
You <i>are</i> friends.

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:46.640
You’re a precious friend to Mieze.

00:15:47.720 --> 00:15:51.400
It only gets so angry
because you’re its friend.

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:53.140
It comes from the heart.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:01.600
Regina!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.480
We were shocked
when the school phoned us.

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:06.220
It happened again?

00:16:07.240 --> 00:16:08.920
Mieze?

00:16:08.920 --> 00:16:11.280
Is Mieze okay?

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.140
So there <i>was</i>
something wrong with Mieze?

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:15.910
No, there’s nothing wrong with it.

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.730
Huh? What do you mean?

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.410
Papa. Mama.

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:28.380
Mieze... was protecting me all along
so I wouldn’t be bullied.

00:16:29.800 --> 00:16:36.650
And... Mieze pushed itself too hard.
It can’t keep going on like this.

00:16:36.650 --> 00:16:40.040
All because
I hid behind Mieze...!

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:43.590
Regina...

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:52.550
So that’s what happened...

00:16:53.220 --> 00:16:56.160
I’m sorry I never realized...

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.170
I’m going to get stronger.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:08.670
I’ll get stronger,
so that I can protect Mieze.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:10.510
That’s the spirit, Regina!

00:17:10.510 --> 00:17:11.280
Great!

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.930
We’ll be cheering for you!

00:17:15.270 --> 00:17:19.180
Thank you,
Go, Satoshi, Koharu.

00:17:21.600 --> 00:17:22.440
Mieze!

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:26.460
What a relief...

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:34.070
So Regina had someone all along.

00:17:34.630 --> 00:17:35.830
She had a friend.

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:44.840
Today, Regina has something
to tell you all.

00:17:47.620 --> 00:17:49.800
Everyone...
I’m very sorry!

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.050
I’ll be more careful
in the future,

00:17:53.050 --> 00:17:56.180
so please forgive
Mieze and I!

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:04.190
That’s not all. Regina and Mieze
have a present for everyone here today.

00:18:05.040 --> 00:18:09.080
Mieze and I like to make
ice theme parks to play in.

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:15.120
I thought that playing together with everyone
would be much, much, <i>much</i> more fun, so let’s make one!

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:17.820
Satoshi and I
are gonna be Regina’s assistants!

00:18:17.820 --> 00:18:20.660
All right!
Come on out, Uonoragon!

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:23.210
You’re up, Dewgong!
Pacchilldon!

00:18:26.710 --> 00:18:28.340
Pacchilldon! Powder Snow!

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:35.090
Uonoragon! Water Gun!

00:18:36.350 --> 00:18:37.220
Mieze!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.100
Dewgong!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:39.600
Icy Wind!

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:51.190
Pacchilldon, use Ice Fang!

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.700
Let’s have fun, everyone!

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:03.960
Woo-hoo!

00:19:05.320 --> 00:19:06.580
Yahoo!

00:19:14.940 --> 00:19:17.140
Let’s put the skate rink here.

00:19:18.290 --> 00:19:21.060
Mieze! Ice Beam!

00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.490
Eevee?

00:19:39.240 --> 00:19:43.370
Sometimes, she manages to pull off
her evolved forms’ moves.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.750
Really?

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:47.620
That’s wonderful!

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:49.640
Yeah!

00:20:13.700 --> 00:20:15.320
Go! Satoshi!

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:22.330
A package arrived
from Regina!

00:20:22.330 --> 00:20:24.150
Let’s have a look...

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:32.540
It’s a snow globe!

00:20:32.540 --> 00:20:34.230
With Mieze inside!

00:20:34.230 --> 00:20:35.840
Oh, it’s so pretty...

00:20:36.690 --> 00:20:38.170
Koharu, what about the letter?

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:39.540
Oh, right!

00:20:41.120 --> 00:20:43.040
“How have you been, Koharu?

00:20:43.040 --> 00:20:45.640
“On that note,
how are Satoshi and Go doing?

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:48.050
“I’ve been doing great.

00:20:48.050 --> 00:20:48.960
“Mieze hasn’t sent out...”

00:20:48.960 --> 00:20:52.010
Mieze hasn’t sent out
a single Blizzard ever since.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:55.830
Oh, I mean those
<i>really</i> powerful Blizzards.

00:20:56.610 --> 00:20:59.740
I’m really into
Pokémon battles now.

00:21:00.870 --> 00:21:02.570
Go, Utsubot!

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:16.050
We’ll come and visit during school break,
so look forward to it!

00:21:16.050 --> 00:21:17.460
“Regina.”

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.970
Of course we will!

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:22.800
So Regina’s started battling.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:24.990
Next time we see her,
we’ll have to...

00:21:24.990 --> 00:21:26.970
Have a battle with her!

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.480
Koharu and Eevee
met Regina and Mieze,

00:21:29.480 --> 00:21:33.350
and witnessed the deep bond
between people and Pokémon.

00:21:34.040 --> 00:21:37.790
“Hopefully someday,
we can be as close as they are...”

00:21:38.480 --> 00:21:41.010
...Koharu thought
to herself.

00:23:07.170 --> 00:23:09.600
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:10.860
Go!

00:23:11.810 --> 00:23:12.830
It’s here!

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:14.660
A Trial Mission!

00:23:14.660 --> 00:23:15.420
Very well.

00:23:15.420 --> 00:23:17.670
I’ll let you borrow
the equipment you need.

00:23:17.670 --> 00:23:18.850
However!

00:23:18.850 --> 00:23:21.170
You have to help out
with my work.

00:23:21.170 --> 00:23:22.390
Work?

00:23:22.390 --> 00:23:24.560
Treasure hunting!

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:27.020
You two’re gonna
make my dreams come true.

00:23:27.020 --> 00:23:29.400
Go catch a wild Kingdra!

00:23:29.400 --> 00:23:31.170
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:34.570
A Trial Mission!
The Deep Sea Diving Research Team!!
